This function uses regression depth via the \code{mrfDepth} package to find
the "deepest" regression hyperplane in the (X, y) space.

The method:
\enumerate{
\item Combines predictors and outcome: \eqn{(X_1, \ldots, X_p, y)}
\item Computes the regression depth median using \code{rdepthmedian()}
\item Returns the deepest hyperplane coefficients
}

\strong{Regression depth} measures how "central" a hyperplane is relative to the
data cloud. The deepest hyperplane is most representative of the overall
data pattern and is highly resistant to outliers.

\strong{Properties}:
\itemize{
\item High breakdown point (up to 33\%)
\item Affine equivariant
\item Robust to outliers in both predictors and outcome
\item No distributional assumptions
